  "modelTests": {
    "passed": 31,
    "reporter": "node-test TAP",
    "testNames": [
      "exact public API, CommonJS/browser equivalence and deeply immutable configuration",
      "all six public cards have exact bounds, starts, powers, bands and independent ranges",
      "fresh state normalizes seed/level without coercion and every layout begins uncaptured",
      "synthetic near-focus poses distinguish signed virtual, focal null and real images",
      "synthetic full authored domain keeps geometry finite and satisfies lens/ray identities",
      "synthetic optical cases keep DIM, OVER, SOFT and no-real-image failures independent",
      "synthetic band equality and either adjacent side use inclusive cross-products",
      "synthetic sequential clarity-only and brightness-only exposures never accumulate a capture",
      "moving either carriage and aperture alters its own current optical measurement",
      "synthetic all end stops block freely, preserve cache and cannot exceed adjustment allowance",
      "three ordinary two-card rounds accept actual observed optics and retain bounded receipts",
      "ordinary first-card success resets every per-card value but retains counters, time and held history",
      "ordinary four rejected exposures lose energy on every initial layout without mechanical cost",
      "ordinary successful final-energy captures advance then win and retain all eight exposures",
      "ordinary exactly-allowed changes still permit exposure; actual extra change applies then loses",
      "synthetic exact adjustment budget can successfully expose, while aperture overrun consumes no energy",
      "synthetic corrupted optics and copied card cannot authorize an invalid capture or change bounds",
      "B>A>direction consumes simultaneous edges and held A permits fresh directions without new exposure",
      "axis threshold/clamp, vertical ties, changed nonneutral directions and no held repeat",
      "fresh held inputs stay quarantined and initial valid epoch is only a baseline",
      "changed epoch neutral cannot rearm that same call; a later genuine neutral is mandatory",
      "cancelled samples always suppress commands and synthetic neutral never releases quarantine",
      "only nonnegative safe integer epochs persist and invalid epochs are ignored",
      "invalid dt and literal paused true preserve all values/references without inappropriate reads",
      "normalization ignores getters, inherited values, pulses and coercible fields; input stays untouched",
      "arrays/functions/primitives and atomic descriptor failure normalize to wholly neutral",
      "prototype pollution cannot supply normalized controls or intercept detached optical receipt writes",
      "synthetic informational elapsed cap and counter saturation never settle the round",
      "receipts, terminal optics, config and independent rounds share no mutable objects",
      "terminal win, energy loss and adjustment loss freeze before reading duration or input",
      "retry and level change allocate a complete original release-gated round after any outcome"
    ],
